{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSWHMxNUqzXjWTwwvSng","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings:**\n- `Shipment.kt:23-27` — `ShipmentStatus` enum with `CREATED`, `CONFIRMED`, `CANCELLED` statuses\n- `ShipmentController.kt:1-56` — existing endpoints for create, getById, list; error handling via exceptions\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27` — in-memory storage using `ConcurrentHashMap`\n- `ApiExceptions.kt:18-24` — `ResourceNotFoundException` (404) and `ConflictException` (409)\n- `ApiError.kt:31-37` — `ErrorCode` enum for machine-readable error codes\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:13-28` — centralized exception-to-response conversion\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n- All error responses use the `ApiError` envelope with a `code` field and `message`\n- HTTP 201 Created for POST operations that create resources\n- `ConflictException` throws HttpStatus.CONFLICT (409)\n- `ResourceNotFoundException` throws HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND (404)\n- Controllers throw exceptions; handlers respond consistently\n- MockMvc tests use `jsonPath()` for assertions on response bodies\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ApiError.kt` — must add `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM` error code to the `ErrorCode` enum (confirming cancelled shipment)\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` — must add the `confirm()` endpoint at `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm`\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — must add tests for the new endpoint's four cases\n\n**Risks:**\n- `Shipment` is an immutable data class; confirming requires creating a new instance with updated status and re-saving\n- Idempotency must be explicit: confirming an already-confirmed shipment must not fail\n- Double-check that CANCELLED status transitions are rejected correctly\n\n**Open questions:** None; the ticket fully specifies all four cases.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM` to the `ErrorCode` enum. This will be thrown when attempting to confirm a shipment that is already `CANCELLED`.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add a new endpoint `confirm()` at the path `/{shipmentId}` with `POST` method that:\n   - Fetches the shipment by ID (throw 404 if not found)\n   - If status is `CREATED`, update to `CONFIRMED` and save\n   - If status is `CONFIRMED`, do nothing (idempotent)\n   - If status is `CANCELLED`, throw `ConflictException` with `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM` code\n   - Return the (possibly updated) shipment with HTTP 200 OK\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add four test cases:\n   - Confirm a shipment in `CREATED` status → moves to `CONFIRMED`\n   - Confirm a shipment already in `CONFIRMED` status → succeeds without change (idempotent)\n   - Confirm a `CANCELLED` shipment → HTTP 409 Conflict\n   - Confirm a non-existent shipment → HTTP 404 Not Found\n\n**Alternative rejected and why:**\n- Could have added a `ConfirmShipmentRequest` DTO, but the endpoint takes no body (just the shipment ID), so a request object adds unnecessary noise. The pattern in this codebase is to not use request objects when the path parameters suffice.\n- Could have made the confirm operation return HTTP 204 No Content, but the requirement states \"returns the shipment\", implying a 200 OK with the body.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n*Case 1: CREATED → CONFIRMED (happy path)*\n- Input: `POST /shipments/S-1/confirm` where S-1 exists in CREATED status\n- Read: Fetch shipment from repository\n- Write: Save new Shipment with status = CONFIRMED\n- Output: HTTP 200 + Shipment JSON body\n\n*Case 2: Already CONFIRMED (idempotent)*\n- Input: `POST /shipments/S-1/confirm` where S-1 exists in CONFIRMED status\n- Read: Fetch shipment from repository\n- Write: No write (shipment already CONFIRMED)\n- Output: HTTP 200 + Shipment JSON body (unchanged)\n\n*Case 3: CANCELLED (conflict)*\n- Input: `POST /shipments/S-1/confirm` where S-1 exists in CANCELLED status\n- Read: Fetch shipment from repository\n- Write: None\n- Output: HTTP 409 Conflict + ApiError body with code = SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM\n- Mechanism: Throw `ConflictException(ErrorCode.SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM, ...)`\n\n*Case 4: Not found*\n- Input: `POST /shipments/missing/confirm` where missing does not exist\n- Read: Attempt to fetch; returns null\n- Write: None\n- Output: HTTP 404 Not Found + ApiError body with code = SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n- Mechanism: Throw `ResourceNotFoundException(ErrorCode.SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, ...)`\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- Test 1: `confirms a shipment in CREATED status` — create a shipment, confirm it, assert status changes to CONFIRMED\n- Test 2: `idempotent confirm of already CONFIRMED shipment` — create, confirm once, confirm again, assert no error and status remains CONFIRMED\n- Test 3: `confirm a CANCELLED shipment returns 409` — insert CANCELLED shipment directly into repository, attempt confirm, assert HTTP 409 and error code\n- Test 4: `confirm unknown shipment returns 404` — attempt to confirm non-existent shipment, assert HTTP 404 and error code\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3295,"cache_read_input_tokens":17933,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3295},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b21ca4e3-798d-4655-8548-5ddd738875ed","uuid":"8418306c-a72c-4055-988b-1c7ac92eb767","timestamp":"2026-09-26T18:14:35.336Z","request_id":"req_011CfSWHM8FrDaNkvX7f7tNK"}
